      "title": "How it works",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "1. Pick a video in Load Video.\n2. Video to GIF searches width, fps and colours for the best-looking GIF under target_size_mb (default 2 MB). Switch mode to quality, balanced or smallest for a single pass.\n3. The GIF previews on the node and is saved to the output folder. The report lists the settings it chose and the size and SSIM against a naive ffmpeg GIF.\n4. Run Timer times the whole run and keeps a history; it works unconnected."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "1. Pick a video in Load Video.\n2. Video to GIF searches width, fps and colours for the best-looking GIF under target_size_mb (default 2 MB). Switch mode to quality, balanced or smallest for a single pass.\n3. The GIF previews on the node and is saved to the output folder. The report lists the settings it chose and the size and SSIM against a naive ffmpeg GIF.\n4. Run Timer times the whole run and keeps a history; it works unconnected."
      },
